      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The historic house sits at 1634 Center Road, a small white clapboard Greek Revival home that houses the society’s research library.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://hinckleytwp.org/community/hinckley-township-ohio-history/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Hinckley remained a wilderness longer than nearby areas because its hilly terrain limited early agriculture, with settlement accelerating after land was divided into 100 plots of 160 acres.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
